# Mandate website: environment variables. Copy to .env.local for local development.
# Never commit real secrets. On Vercel, set these under Project Settings > Environment Variables.

# --- Required everywhere -----------------------------------------------------------------
# 32 random bytes, base64. Encrypts every issuer private key at rest (sandboxes and
# organisations). New name: MANDATE_KEY_ENCRYPTION_KEY; the old name MANDATE_SANDBOX_KEY still
# works. Set only one of them (moving over: give the new name the same value).
# Generate: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64'))"
MANDATE_SANDBOX_KEY=
# MANDATE_KEY_ENCRYPTION_KEY=
# At least 32 random characters. Signs sign-in session cookies.
MANDATE_SESSION_SECRET=

# --- Private preview gate (optional) -------------------------------------------------------
# When set, every page asks for this password first. Remove it to make the site public.
SITE_PASSWORD=

# --- Storage ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Postgres connection string (Supabase: Project Settings > Database > Connection string,
# "Transaction pooler", port 6543). When empty, a local embedded database is used instead.
DATABASE_URL=
# Local embedded database folder (development only). Default: web/.data/pglite
# MANDATE_PGLITE_DIR=

# --- Sign-in ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Development only: "1" lets you sign in with any email, no verification. Ignored in production.
MANDATE_DEV_LOGIN=
# Supabase Auth (email sign-in link, PKCE). Public by design; see web/README.md.
# The site's public origin for sign-in links (optional; default: the request's host):
# MANDATE_SITE_URL=https://flow-e.vercel.app
# Mandate project (Central EU, Zurich):
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://khxqgpbgijnhckwlkorg.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable__LHTIX5Dmr0Fg1ctdUztJA_Ak2sFoKm

# --- Email (organisations: invitations and approval links) -------------------------------------
# Development: leave both empty; emails land in the database and show at /dev/outbox
# (needs MANDATE_DEV_LOGIN=1). Production refuses that outbox. Set both to send real email
# through Resend; the sender's domain must be verified in Resend. Setting only one makes
# sending fail on purpose.
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_...
# EMAIL_FROM=Mandate <approvals@example.com>

# --- Pilot requests (home page form) ----------------------------------------------------------
# One address that gets an email per pilot request (development: lands in /dev/outbox).
# MANDATE_LEADS_TO=
# Comma-separated emails that may open /admin/pilots after signing in. Unset: nobody.
# MANDATE_ADMIN_EMAILS=
